---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: Astro uses this layout component below.
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Docs | plansplease"
  description="Short guides for the plansplease CLI and private cloud workspace."
  activePath="docs"
>
  <section class="page-heading" aria-labelledby="docs-title">
    <div>
      <h1 id="docs-title">Docs for a small tool.</h1>
      <p>
        The alpha has two paths. Run a page locally with the CLI, or save one standalone HTML file
        in your private cloud workspace.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="page-action" href="../cli/">Start with the CLI</a>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="docs-list-title">
    <h2 id="docs-list-title">Start here.</h2>

    <div class="feature-list">
      <article class="feature-row">
        <span class="feature-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Install the CLI</h2>
          <p>Install the command once, then give an HTML file a local URL whenever an agent makes one.</p>
        </div>
        <code class="feature-command">npm install --global @abijith-suresh/planview</code>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-row">
        <span class="feature-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Publish a local page</h2>
          <p>
            Publish a file or page folder. The CLI keeps the snapshot on your machine and prints the
            URL.
          </p>
        </div>
        <code class="feature-command">planview publish --open ./page.html</code>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-row">
        <span class="feature-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Save a cloud copy</h2>
          <p>
            Sign in to the staging app and upload one standalone HTML file. The current cloud
            workflow does not accept bundled assets yet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="feature-command">private / one file</span>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="page-note">
      More detailed API and self-hosting docs will come after the alpha workflow settles.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
